The common entity handles of an embedded MTEXT (ATTRIB, ATTDEF,
GEOPOSITIONMARKER since R2010) read num_reactors handles without checking
the end of the handle stream. A corrupt num_reactors (up to 2^32) then reads
past the end billions of times, each logging an error: the decoder hangs.
Stop at the first handle that cannot be read.

diff --git a/src/dwg_spec_shared.h b/src/dwg_spec_shared.h
index d720a4f..9b8a98f 100644
--- a/src/dwg_spec_shared.h
+++ b/src/dwg_spec_shared.h
@@ -740,7 +740,8 @@ free_3dsolid (Dwg_Object *restrict obj, Dwg_Entity_3DSOLID *restrict _obj)
                (BITCODE_BL)SUB_FIELD_VALUE (mtext,          \
                                            num_reactors);    \
            vcount++)                                         \
-        bit_read_H (hdl_dat, &htmp); /* reactors */          \
+        if (bit_read_H (hdl_dat, &htmp)) /* reactors */      \
+          break; /* end of the handle stream */              \
     }                                                        \
   SINCE (R_2004a)                                            \
     {                                                        \
